From: DashBerry <zero/README.md>
Subject: [PATCH] configfs: discover formats from the real tree, not the symlinks

uvc-gadget finds its formats by ftw()-ing configfs and matching paths that
contain "streaming/class/". Those paths exist only through symlinks:

    streaming/class/<speed>/<header>  ->  streaming/header/<header>
    streaming/header/<header>/<inst>  ->  streaming/<format>/<inst>

and ftw() does not descend into them on configfs. Measured on the device with
the diagnostics from 0002:

    ftw returned 0 (errno 0: none); files seen 122, under streaming/class 0

122 files walked, not one under streaming/class - while find -follow reaches
them and cat reads through them fine. So no format is ever recorded, and the
only symptom is "configfs settings for uvc gadget not found".

The real path carries everything except the speed:

    .../streaming/<format>/<instance>/<frame>/<attribute>

so this matches that shape as well and registers each frame for fs, hs and ss.
That is not an assumption: multi-gadget.sh links the same header into all three
class/<speed> groups, so every format really is offered at every speed, and the
result is what walking the class/ view would have produced.

Only 4-component paths are used - format/instance/frame/attribute. Shorter ones
are format- or header-level attributes with no frame to belong to, and feeding
them in would produce noise from the value parser.

NOT EXPLAINED: the same binary at the same SHA is said to work on a stock
5.10 card with the same tree shape. If ftw() behaved differently there, this
change is harmless on it - the class/ branch still runs first and this one only
adds paths it would otherwise ignore.
---
diff --git a/uvc-gadget.c b/uvc-gadget.c
index b16475a..15a4f86 100644
--- a/uvc-gadget.c
+++ b/uvc-gadget.c
@@ -2211,10 +2211,55 @@ static void configfs_fill_streaming_params(const char* path, const char * part)
 static int dashberry_files_seen = 0;
 static int dashberry_files_matched = 0;
 
+/* DashBerry: discover formats from the REAL directories, not the class/ view.
+ *
+ * configfs exposes the streaming formats twice: once at their real path,
+ *     .../streaming/<format>/<instance>/<frame>/<attribute>
+ * and once through symlinks under
+ *     .../streaming/class/<speed>/<header>/<instance>/<frame>/<attribute>
+ * and this walk only ever matched the second. ftw() does not descend into
+ * those symlinks on configfs - measured on the device: 122 files seen, 0
+ * under streaming/class - so no format was ever recorded and the only
+ * symptom was "configfs settings for uvc gadget not found".
+ *
+ * The real path carries everything except the speed. multi-gadget.sh links
+ * the same header into class/fs, class/hs and class/ss, so every format is
+ * available at every speed, and the entry is registered for each in turn -
+ * which is exactly what walking the class/ view would have produced.
+ */
+static void configfs_fill_formats_real(const char * path, const char * part)
+{
+    static const char * const speeds[] = { "fs", "hs", "ss" };
+    char synth[256];
+    char * copy = strdup(part);
+    char * tok = strtok(copy, "/");
+    char * arr[8];
+    int n = 0;
+    unsigned int i;
+
+    while (tok != NULL && n < 8) {
+        arr[n++] = tok;
+        tok = strtok(NULL, "/");
+    }
+
+    /* <format>/<instance>/<frame>/<attribute> only: anything shorter is a
+     * format- or header-level attribute and has no frame to belong to. */
+    if (n == 4) {
+        for (i = 0; i < sizeof(speeds) / sizeof(speeds[0]); i++) {
+            snprintf(synth, sizeof(synth), "%s/h/%s/%s/%s",
+                     speeds[i], arr[1], arr[2], arr[3]);
+            configfs_fill_formats(path, synth);
+        }
+    }
+
+    free(copy);
+}
+
 static int configfs_path_check(const char* fpath, const struct stat * sb, int tflag)
 {
     int uvc = find_text_pos(fpath, "/uvc");
     int streaming = find_text_pos(fpath, "streaming/class/");
+    int streaming_real = find_text_pos(fpath, "/streaming/");
     int streaming_params = find_text_pos(fpath, "/streaming_");
     (void)(tflag); /* avoid warning: unused parameter 'tflag' */
 
@@ -2224,6 +2269,10 @@ static int configfs_path_check(const char* fpath, const struct stat * sb, int tf
             dashberry_files_matched++;
             configfs_fill_formats(fpath, fpath + streaming + 16);
 
+        } else if (streaming_real && uvc) {
+            dashberry_files_matched++;
+            configfs_fill_formats_real(fpath, fpath + streaming_real + 11);
+
         } else if (streaming_params) {
             configfs_fill_streaming_params(fpath, fpath + streaming_params + 11);
 
